{% set local_problem %}
<p>Trinity's varied terrain creates different drainage challenges. Some properties have grading that directs water toward homes rather than away. Others have soil conditions that prevent proper absorption.</p>

<p>Surface solutions have limits. Splash blocks move water a few inches. Extensions move it a few feet. But on many properties, that's not far enough.</p>

<p>We've seen the results: wet basements, crawlspace moisture, foundation cracks. Homeowners try various surface solutions without lasting success because the fundamental problem isn't addressed.</p>

<p>Underground drains solve this permanently. Buried pipes carry water far enough away that it can never threaten your home.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Underground drains are buried pipes that connect to your downspouts and carry water to a discharge point far from your home. We use 4-inch corrugated or solid PVC pipe with proper slope to ensure continuous flow.</p>

<p>Unlike French drains (which collect groundwater), underground gutter drains handle roof runoff before it reaches the ground. They work with your gutter system for complete water management.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've installed underground drainage systems throughout Morgan County for over 20 years. We understand local soil conditions and what actually works.</p>

<p>We're just 10 miles away in Hartselle — your closest gutter company. When we install a system for a Trinity neighbor, we know we'll be around for years to come.</p>
{% endset %}
